{# A contract sent and not signed, chased once more.

   It carries a *new* address and says so. The previous one is revoked by the
   same act, because the application never keeps the token it handed out: it
   stores only a hash of it, so a reminder that pointed at the old address
   would be a link the application itself cannot build. Saying which address
   counts is therefore not politeness, it is the only honest thing to say. #}
<p>{{ 'studio.email.contract_reminder.body'|trans({'{reference}': contract.reference}) }}</p>

<p><a href="{{ url }}">{{ 'studio.email.contract_reminder.cta'|trans }}</a></p>

<p>{{ 'studio.email.contract_reminder.replaces'|trans }}</p>

<p>{{ 'studio.email.contract_reminder.expires'|trans({'{date}': expiresAt|site_date}) }}</p>
